IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`
IMPORT `sfaa-div1-interpretation`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, Part 7 Division 1 Subdivision (1): disclosure by directors and chief executive officers of a corporation (sections 133 and 134).
-- "Corporation" here is the listed body of section 130(2): the caller says whether the body is one (`the body is a corporation within section 130(2)`).
-- Business days (the 2-business-day limits) are counted by sfa-periods.l4 (convention P8). A notice given on the very day the person becomes aware is in time:
-- the last day is compared with AT MOST rather than with the window function that opens the day after the event (fork register A3).

§ `s 133: duty of a director or chief executive officer to notify the corporation of his or her interests`

-- The matters of paragraph (1): (a) to (e) each name the corporation (sub-paragraph (i)) or a related corporation (sub-paragraph (ii)); (f) is what the Authority prescribes.
-- (g), a change in the particulars of any of them, is the flag `the notice is of a change in the particulars of the matter` with the matter changed.
DECLARE `s 133(1) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 133(1)(a)(i) shares in the corporation`
    `s 133(1)(a)(ii) shares in a related corporation of the corporation`
    `s 133(1)(b)(i) debentures of the corporation`
    `s 133(1)(b)(ii) debentures of a related corporation of the corporation`
    `s 133(1)(c)(i) rights or options in respect of the acquisition or disposal of shares in or debentures of the corporation`
    `s 133(1)(c)(ii) rights or options in respect of the acquisition or disposal of shares in or debentures of a related corporation`
    `s 133(1)(d)(i) contracts under which a person has a right to call for or make delivery of shares in the corporation`
    `s 133(1)(d)(ii) contracts under which a person has a right to call for or make delivery of shares in a related corporation`
    `s 133(1)(e)(i) participatory interests made available by the corporation`
    `s 133(1)(e)(ii) participatory interests made available by a related corporation`
    `s 133(1)(f) other securities or securities-based derivatives contracts the Authority prescribes`

-- Subsection (2): the related-corporation paragraphs, paragraph (e) and a change in them "only apply to a director of a corporation which is a company".
-- The paragraph is closed with "only", so a chief executive officer, or a director of a non-company, is outside it: JUST FALSE.
-- src:28188 | (2) Paragraphs (a)(ii), (b)(ii), (c)(ii), (d)(ii), (e) and (g) (in respect
-- src:28189 | of a change in the particulars of any matter referred to in
-- src:28190 | paragraphs (a)(ii), (b)(ii), (c)(ii), (d)(ii) and (e)) of subsection (1)
-- src:28191 | only apply to a director of a corporation which is a company.
@ref s 133(2) (src:28188-28191)
GIVEN
    `the matter` IS A `s 133(1) matter` @desc Which kind of matter is it: shares, debentures, rights or options, contracts, participatory interests, or other securities that the Authority prescribes, of the corporation or of a related corporation?
    `the person is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director of the corporation (as section 2(1) defines "director")?
    `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a company (as section 2(1) defines "company")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(2) the paragraph applies to a director of a corporation which is a company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `s 133(1)(a)(ii) shares in a related corporation of the corporation` THEN `s 133(2) the person is a director of a company` `the person is a director of the corporation` `the body is a company`
    WHEN `s 133(1)(b)(ii) debentures of a related corporation of the corporation` THEN `s 133(2) the person is a director of a company` `the person is a director of the corporation` `the body is a company`
    WHEN `s 133(1)(c)(ii) rights or options in respect of the acquisition or disposal of shares in or debentures of a related corporation` THEN `s 133(2) the person is a director of a company` `the person is a director of the corporation` `the body is a company`
    WHEN `s 133(1)(d)(ii) contracts under which a person has a right to call for or make delivery of shares in a related corporation` THEN `s 133(2) the person is a director of a company` `the person is a director of the corporation` `the body is a company`
    WHEN `s 133(1)(e)(i) participatory interests made available by the corporation` THEN `s 133(2) the person is a director of a company` `the person is a director of the corporation` `the body is a company`
    WHEN `s 133(1)(e)(ii) participatory interests made available by a related corporation` THEN `s 133(2) the person is a director of a company` `the person is a director of the corporation` `the body is a company`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (2) names paragraphs (a)(ii), (b)(ii), (c)(ii), (d)(ii), (e) and (g) in respect of them; this matter is not among them

-- The one test behind every limited paragraph of subsection (2).
-- src:28188 | (2) Paragraphs (a)(ii), (b)(ii), (c)(ii), (d)(ii), (e) and (g) (in respect
-- src:28189 | of a change in the particulars of any matter referred to in
-- src:28190 | paragraphs (a)(ii), (b)(ii), (c)(ii), (d)(ii) and (e)) of subsection (1)
-- src:28191 | only apply to a director of a corporation which is a company.
@ref 2 s 133(2) (the test) (src:28188-28191)
GIVEN
    `the person is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director of the corporation (as section 2(1) defines "director")?
    `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a company (as section 2(1) defines "company")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(2) the person is a director of a company` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of the corporation` AND `the body is a company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only apply to a director of a corporation which is a company"

-- src:28126 | 133.—(1) Every director and chief executive officer of a
-- src:28127 | corporation must give written notice to the corporation of
-- src:28128 | particulars of —
-- src:28130 | (a) shares in ––
-- src:28132 | (i) the corporation; or
-- src:28134 | (ii) a related corporation of the corporation,
-- src:28136 | (a) which he or she holds, or in which he or she has an interest
-- src:28137 | and the nature and extent of that interest;
-- src:28139 | (b) debentures of —
-- src:28141 | (i) the corporation; or
-- src:28143 | (ii) a related corporation of the corporation,
-- src:28145 | (b) which he or she holds, or in which he or she has an interest
-- src:28146 | and the nature and extent of that interest;
-- src:28148 | (c) his or her rights or options, or rights or options of his or
-- src:28149 | hers and another person or other persons, in respect of the
-- src:28150 | acquisition or disposal of shares in or debentures of —
-- src:28152 | (i) the corporation; or
-- src:28154 | (ii) a related corporation of the corporation;
-- src:28156 | (d) contracts to which he or she is a party, or under which he or
-- src:28157 | she is entitled to a benefit, being contracts under which a
-- src:28158 | person has a right to call for or to make delivery of shares
-- src:28159 | in ––
-- src:28161 | (i) the corporation; or
-- src:28163 | (ii) a related corporation of the corporation;
-- src:28165 | (e) participatory interests made available by —
-- src:28167 | (i) the corporation; or
-- src:28172 | (ii) a related corporation of the corporation,
-- src:28174 | (e) which he or she holds, or in which he or she has an interest
-- src:28175 | and the nature and extent of that interest;
-- src:28177 | (f) such other securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:28178 | contracts as the Authority may prescribe, which are held,
-- src:28179 | whether directly or indirectly, by him or her, or in which he
-- src:28180 | or she has an interest and the nature and extent of that
-- src:28181 | interest; and
-- src:28183 | (g) any change in respect of the particulars of any matter
-- src:28184 | referred to in paragraphs (a) to (f).
@ref s 133(1) (src:28126-28184)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
    `the person is a director of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director of the corporation (as section 2(1) defines "director")?
    `the person is a chief executive officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the chief executive officer of the corporation (as section 2(1) defines "chief executive officer")?
    `the body is a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a company (as section 2(1) defines "company")?
    `the matter` IS A `s 133(1) matter` @desc Which kind of matter is it: shares, debentures, rights or options, contracts, participatory interests, or other securities that the Authority prescribes, of the corporation or of a related corporation?
    `the person holds or has an interest in the matter, or the particulars of it have changed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person hold, or have an interest in, the matter (or have the rights, options or contracts), or have the particulars of it changed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(1) the director or chief executive officer must give the corporation written notice of the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every director and chief executive officer of a corporation"; the body is not a corporation as section 130(2) reads the word for Division 1
        IF NOT (`the person is a director of the corporation` OR `the person is a chief executive officer of the corporation`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every director and chief executive officer of a corporation must give written notice"
        IF `s 133(2) the paragraph applies to a director of a corporation which is a company` `the matter` `the person is a director of the corporation` `the body is a company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only apply to a director of a corporation which is a company"
        IF NOT `the person holds or has an interest in the matter, or the particulars of it have changed`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "particulars of" the shares, debentures and the rest "which he or she holds, or in which he or she has an interest"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Subsection (3)(a): the form and information are the Authority's to prescribe, so what they are is an input.
-- src:28195 | (3) A notice under subsection (1) —
-- src:28197 | (a) must be in such form and must contain such information as
-- src:28198 | the Authority may prescribe; and
@ref s 133(3)(a) (src:28195-28198)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has prescribed the form and the information for the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed a form for the notice and the information it must contain?
    `the notice is in the form the Authority prescribes and contains the information it prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice in the form the Authority has prescribed, and does it contain the information the Authority has prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(3)(a) the notice is in the form and contains the information the Authority prescribes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Authority has prescribed the form and the information for the notice`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "as the Authority may prescribe"
        IF `the notice is in the form the Authority prescribes and contains the information it prescribes`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be in such form and must contain such information as the Authority may prescribe"

-- Subsection (3)(b): the time. (i) a change: 2 business days after the person becomes aware (s 130(6) fixes when a person "becomes aware");
-- (ii) any other case: 2 business days after the LATER of (A) becoming director or chief executive officer and (B) becoming a holder of, or acquiring an interest in, the matter.
-- src:28200 | (b) must be given —
-- src:28202 | (i) in the case of a notice under subsection (1)(g), within
-- src:28203 | 2 business days after the director or chief executive
-- src:28204 | officer becomes aware of the change; or
@ref s 133(3)(b)(i) (src:28200-28204)
GIVEN
    `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person actually become aware of the fact or occurrence?
    `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of the fact or occurrence if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of their affairs?
    `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which dates in the period were there public holidays in Singapore? (Saturdays and Sundays are counted automatically.)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 133(3)(b)(i) the last day for the notice of a change` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a number of business days after` (`s 130(6) the day from which the person is taken to have been aware` `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence`) 2 `the public holidays`

-- src:28206 | (ii) in any other case, within 2 business days after —
-- src:28208 | (A) the date on which the director or chief
-- src:28209 | executive officer becomes such a director or
-- src:28210 | chief executive officer; or
-- src:28212 | (B) the date on which the director or chief
-- src:28213 | executive officer becomes a holder of, or
-- src:28214 | acquires an interest in, the shares, debentures,
-- src:28215 | rights, options, contracts, participatory
-- src:28216 | interests, other securities or securities‑based
-- src:28217 | derivatives contracts referred to in
-- src:28218 | subsection (1),
-- src:28223 | (ii) whichever last occurs. [2/2009; 4/2017]
@ref s 133(3)(b)(ii) (src:28206-28223)
GIVEN
    `the day the person becomes director or chief executive officer` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person become a director or chief executive officer of the corporation?
    `the day the person becomes a holder of, or acquires an interest in, the matter` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person become a holder of, or acquire an interest in, the matter?
    `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which dates in the period were there public holidays in Singapore? (Saturdays and Sundays are counted automatically.)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 133(3)(b)(ii) the last day for any other notice` MEANS
    -- "whichever last occurs": the later of the two dates starts the 2 business days
    IF `the day the person becomes a holder of, or acquires an interest in, the matter` GREATER THAN `the day the person becomes director or chief executive officer`
    THEN `period: the last day of a number of business days after` `the day the person becomes a holder of, or acquires an interest in, the matter` 2 `the public holidays`
    ELSE `period: the last day of a number of business days after` `the day the person becomes director or chief executive officer` 2 `the public holidays`

-- src:28200 | (b) must be given —
-- src:28202 | (i) in the case of a notice under subsection (1)(g), within
-- src:28203 | 2 business days after the director or chief executive
-- src:28204 | officer becomes aware of the change; or
-- src:28206 | (ii) in any other case, within 2 business days after —
-- src:28208 | (A) the date on which the director or chief
-- src:28209 | executive officer becomes such a director or
-- src:28210 | chief executive officer; or
-- src:28212 | (B) the date on which the director or chief
-- src:28213 | executive officer becomes a holder of, or
-- src:28214 | acquires an interest in, the shares, debentures,
-- src:28215 | rights, options, contracts, participatory
-- src:28216 | interests, other securities or securities‑based
-- src:28217 | derivatives contracts referred to in
-- src:28218 | subsection (1),
-- src:28223 | (ii) whichever last occurs. [2/2009; 4/2017]
@ref s 133(3)(b) (src:28200-28223)
GIVEN
    `the notice is of a change in the particulars of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice of a change in the particulars of that matter (paragraph (g))?
    `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person actually become aware of the fact or occurrence?
    `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest date on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager as the case may be, would have become aware of the fact or occurrence if acting with reasonable diligence in the conduct of their affairs?
    `the day the person becomes director or chief executive officer` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person become a director or chief executive officer of the corporation?
    `the day the person becomes a holder of, or acquires an interest in, the matter` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the person become a holder of, or acquire an interest in, the matter?
    `the day the notice is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice given?
    `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc On which dates in the period were there public holidays in Singapore? (Saturdays and Sundays are counted automatically.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(3)(b) the notice is given in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice is given` AT MOST (IF `the notice is of a change in the particulars of the matter` THEN `s 133(3)(b)(i) the last day for the notice of a change` `the day the person actually became aware of the fact or occurrence` `the earliest day on which the person, or the person's officer, partner or manager, would have become aware of it if acting with reasonable diligence` `the public holidays` ELSE `s 133(3)(b)(ii) the last day for any other notice` `the day the person becomes director or chief executive officer` `the day the person becomes a holder of, or acquires an interest in, the matter` `the public holidays`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be given within 2 business days after"; a period fixed in the text's own words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a))

-- Subsection (6): "family member" means a spouse, or a son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter or stepdaughter below the age of 21 years.
-- Fork register A2: "below the age of 21 years" is read as limiting the children, not the spouse.
-- src:28267 | (6) In this section, “family member” means a spouse, or a son,
-- src:28268 | adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter or stepdaughter
-- src:28269 | below the age of 21 years.
@ref s 133(6) (src:28267-28269)
GIVEN
    `the relation of the person to the director or chief executive officer` IS A `Family relation` @desc What is the person's relation to the director or chief executive officer?
    `the age of the relation in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is that relation, in years?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(6) "family member" the person is a family member` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relation of the person to the director or chief executive officer`
    WHEN `a spouse` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a son` THEN `s 133(6) the child is below the age of 21 years` `the age of the relation in years`
    WHEN `an adopted son` THEN `s 133(6) the child is below the age of 21 years` `the age of the relation in years`
    WHEN `a stepson` THEN `s 133(6) the child is below the age of 21 years` `the age of the relation in years`
    WHEN `a daughter` THEN `s 133(6) the child is below the age of 21 years` `the age of the relation in years`
    WHEN `an adopted daughter` THEN `s 133(6) the child is below the age of 21 years` `the age of the relation in years`
    WHEN `a stepdaughter` THEN `s 133(6) the child is below the age of 21 years` `the age of the relation in years`
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a spouse, or a son, adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter or stepdaughter below the age of 21 years"

-- src:28267 | (6) In this section, “family member” means a spouse, or a son,
-- src:28268 | adopted son, stepson, daughter, adopted daughter or stepdaughter
-- src:28269 | below the age of 21 years.
@ref 2 s 133(6) (the age limit on a child) (src:28267-28269)
GIVEN
    `the age of the relation in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is that relation, in years?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(6) the child is below the age of 21 years` MEANS
    IF `the age of the relation in years` LESS THAN 21
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "below the age of 21 years"

-- Subsection (4)(a): a deemed interest. The text introduces it with "if", so a family member who holds nothing gives JUST FALSE (marginal reading (a), listed in NOTES.md);
-- the carve-out "(not being himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation)" and the defined term are limits in the text's own wording: NOTHING outside them.
-- src:28226 | (a) a director or chief executive officer of a corporation is
-- src:28227 | deemed to have an interest in securities or securities‑based
-- src:28228 | derivatives contracts referred to in subsection (1) if a
-- src:28229 | family member of the director or chief executive officer
-- src:28230 | (not being himself or herself a director or chief executive
-- src:28231 | officer of the corporation) (as the case may be) holds or has
-- src:28232 | an interest in those securities or securities‑based
-- src:28233 | derivatives contracts; and
@ref s 133(4)(a) (src:28226-28233)
GIVEN
    `the person is a family member of the director or chief executive officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 133(6) answer for the person (a spouse, or a child below 21)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the family member is himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the family member himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation?
    `the family member holds or has an interest in those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the family member hold, or have an interest in, those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(4)(a) the director or chief executive officer is deemed to have the family member's interest` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person is a family member of the director or chief executive officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (NOT `the family member is himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation`) AND `the family member holds or has an interest in those securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the person is a family member of the director or chief executive officer` EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR `the family member is himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a family member of the director or chief executive officer (not being himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation)"
        IF `the person is a family member of the director or chief executive officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to have an interest in securities or securities-based derivatives contracts referred to in subsection (1) if a family member"
        -- MARGINAL-READING (a): the deeming rule is introduced with "if"; a failed "if" is taken as the text's no. The other reading is NOTHING.
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the answer for "family member" was not given

-- src:28235 | (b) any contract entered into by, any assignment or right of
-- src:28236 | subscription made or exercised by, or any grant made to, a
-- src:28237 | family member of a director or chief executive officer of a
-- src:28238 | corporation (not being himself or herself a director or chief
-- src:28239 | executive officer of the corporation) is deemed to have
-- src:28240 | been entered into by, made or exercised by or made to the
-- src:28241 | director or chief executive officer.
@ref s 133(4)(b) (src:28235-28241)
GIVEN
    `the person is a family member of the director or chief executive officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 133(6) answer for the person (a spouse, or a child below 21)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the family member is himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the family member himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation?
    `the act is a contract entered into by, an assignment or right of subscription made or exercised by, or a grant made to, the family member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act a contract entered into by, an assignment or right of subscription made or exercised by, or a grant made to, the family member?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(4)(b) the family member's contract, assignment, right of subscription or grant is deemed to be the director's or chief executive officer's` MEANS
    IF (`the person is a family member of the director or chief executive officer` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (NOT `the family member is himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation`) AND `the act is a contract entered into by, an assignment or right of subscription made or exercised by, or a grant made to, the family member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a family member of a director or chief executive officer of a corporation (not being himself or herself a director or chief executive officer of the corporation)"

-- src:28247 | (a) a reference to a participatory interest is a reference to a unit
-- src:28248 | in a collective investment scheme; and
@ref s 133(5)(a) (src:28247-28248)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a unit in a collective investment scheme (as section 2(1) defines "unit")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(5)(a) the thing is a participatory interest` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a unit in a collective investment scheme`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a reference to a participatory interest is a reference to a unit in a collective investment scheme"

-- src:28250 | (b) a reference to a person who holds or acquires participatory
-- src:28251 | interests, other securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:28252 | contracts referred to in subsection (1), or an interest in
-- src:28253 | shares, debentures, participatory interests, other securities
-- src:28254 | or securities‑based derivatives contracts referred to in that
-- src:28255 | subsection, includes a reference to a person who under an
-- src:28256 | option holds or acquires a right to acquire or dispose of the
-- src:28257 | participatory interests, securities or securities‑based
-- src:28258 | derivatives contracts, or the interest in shares,
-- src:28259 | debentures, participatory interests, securities or
-- src:28260 | securities‑based derivatives contracts.
@ref s 133(5)(b) (src:28250-28260)
GIVEN
    `the person under an option holds or acquires a right to acquire or dispose of the interests, securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person, under an option, hold or acquire a right to acquire or dispose of the participatory interests, securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, or of an interest in them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 133(5)(b) the person who under an option holds or acquires a right is included among those who hold or acquire` MEANS
    IF `the person under an option holds or acquires a right to acquire or dispose of the interests, securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to a person who under an option holds or acquires a right"; the ordinary sense of "holds or acquires" is not closed off

-- The regulative rule for the notice: the director or chief executive officer MUST give written notice within 2 business days (the clock of a trace counts business days
-- after the trigger; the dates are counted by the decision functions above). The party is an input so that one rule serves the director and the chief executive officer.
DECLARE `s 133 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 133 give the corporation written notice`

-- src:28126 | 133.—(1) Every director and chief executive officer of a
-- src:28127 | corporation must give written notice to the corporation of
-- src:28128 | particulars of —
-- src:28130 | (a) shares in ––
-- src:28132 | (i) the corporation; or
-- src:28134 | (ii) a related corporation of the corporation,
-- src:28136 | (a) which he or she holds, or in which he or she has an interest
-- src:28137 | and the nature and extent of that interest;
-- src:28139 | (b) debentures of —
-- src:28141 | (i) the corporation; or
-- src:28143 | (ii) a related corporation of the corporation,
-- src:28145 | (b) which he or she holds, or in which he or she has an interest
-- src:28146 | and the nature and extent of that interest;
-- src:28148 | (c) his or her rights or options, or rights or options of his or
-- src:28149 | hers and another person or other persons, in respect of the
-- src:28150 | acquisition or disposal of shares in or debentures of —
-- src:28152 | (i) the corporation; or
-- src:28154 | (ii) a related corporation of the corporation;
-- src:28156 | (d) contracts to which he or she is a party, or under which he or
-- src:28157 | she is entitled to a benefit, being contracts under which a
-- src:28158 | person has a right to call for or to make delivery of shares
-- src:28159 | in ––
-- src:28161 | (i) the corporation; or
-- src:28163 | (ii) a related corporation of the corporation;
-- src:28165 | (e) participatory interests made available by —
-- src:28167 | (i) the corporation; or
-- src:28172 | (ii) a related corporation of the corporation,
-- src:28174 | (e) which he or she holds, or in which he or she has an interest
-- src:28175 | and the nature and extent of that interest;
-- src:28177 | (f) such other securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:28178 | contracts as the Authority may prescribe, which are held,
-- src:28179 | whether directly or indirectly, by him or her, or in which he
-- src:28180 | or she has an interest and the nature and extent of that
-- src:28181 | interest; and
-- src:28183 | (g) any change in respect of the particulars of any matter
-- src:28184 | referred to in paragraphs (a) to (f).
-- src:28188 | (2) Paragraphs (a)(ii), (b)(ii), (c)(ii), (d)(ii), (e) and (g) (in respect
-- src:28189 | of a change in the particulars of any matter referred to in
-- src:28190 | paragraphs (a)(ii), (b)(ii), (c)(ii), (d)(ii) and (e)) of subsection (1)
-- src:28191 | only apply to a director of a corporation which is a company.
-- src:28195 | (3) A notice under subsection (1) —
-- src:28197 | (a) must be in such form and must contain such information as
-- src:28198 | the Authority may prescribe; and
-- src:28200 | (b) must be given —
-- src:28202 | (i) in the case of a notice under subsection (1)(g), within
-- src:28203 | 2 business days after the director or chief executive
-- src:28204 | officer becomes aware of the change; or
-- src:28206 | (ii) in any other case, within 2 business days after —
-- src:28208 | (A) the date on which the director or chief
-- src:28209 | executive officer becomes such a director or
-- src:28210 | chief executive officer; or
-- src:28212 | (B) the date on which the director or chief
-- src:28213 | executive officer becomes a holder of, or
-- src:28214 | acquires an interest in, the shares, debentures,
-- src:28215 | rights, options, contracts, participatory
-- src:28216 | interests, other securities or securities‑based
-- src:28217 | derivatives contracts referred to in
-- src:28218 | subsection (1),
-- src:28223 | (ii) whichever last occurs. [2/2009; 4/2017]
@ref s 133(1) and (3) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:28126-28223)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 133 action`
`s 133(1) and (3) the director or chief executive officer must give written notice within 2 business days` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 133 give the corporation written notice`
    WITHIN 2
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "written notice was not given to the corporation within 2 business days (section 133(3)(b))"

§ `s 134: penalties under Subdivision (1)`

-- The paragraphs of s 133(1) that subsection (1) of s 134 names: (a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) and (f), and (g) in respect of a change in the same.
-- A matter outside the list (a related corporation's, or paragraph (e)) falls to subsection (2) only.
-- src:28278 | (a) intentionally or recklessly contravenes
-- src:28280 | section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) or (f), or
-- src:28282 | section 133(1)(g) in respect of a change in the particulars
-- src:28284 | of any matter referred to in section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i),
-- src:28286 | (c)(i), (d)(i) and (f);
@ref s 134(1) (the matters it names) (src:28278-28286)
GIVEN
    `the matter` IS A `s 133(1) matter` @desc Which kind of matter is it: shares, debentures, rights or options, contracts, participatory interests, or other securities that the Authority prescribes, of the corporation or of a related corporation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 134(1) the matter is one that subsection (1) names` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `s 133(1)(a)(i) shares in the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1)(b)(i) debentures of the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1)(c)(i) rights or options in respect of the acquisition or disposal of shares in or debentures of the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1)(d)(i) contracts under which a person has a right to call for or make delivery of shares in the corporation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1)(f) other securities or securities-based derivatives contracts the Authority prescribes` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:28278 | (a) intentionally or recklessly contravenes
-- src:28280 | section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) or (f), or
-- src:28282 | section 133(1)(g) in respect of a change in the particulars
-- src:28284 | of any matter referred to in section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i),
-- src:28286 | (c)(i), (d)(i) and (f);
@ref s 134(1)(a) (src:28278-28286)
GIVEN
    `the matter` IS A `s 133(1) matter` @desc Which kind of matter is it: shares, debentures, rights or options, contracts, participatory interests, or other securities that the Authority prescribes, of the corporation or of a related corporation?
    `the person contravened section 133(1) in respect of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person fail to give the written notice that section 133(1) requires for the matter?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(1)(a) the director or chief executive officer intentionally or recklessly contravened section 133(1)` MEANS
    IF `s 134(1) the matter is one that subsection (1) names` `the matter` AND `the person contravened section 133(1) in respect of the matter` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("intentionally or recklessly contravenes section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) or (f)"), not that anyone else is innocent

-- src:28288 | (b) intentionally or recklessly contravenes section 133(3) in
-- src:28289 | respect of a notice of the particulars of any matter referred
-- src:28290 | to in section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) and (f) or of a
-- src:28291 | change in any of those particulars; or
@ref s 134(1)(b) (src:28288-28291)
GIVEN
    `the matter` IS A `s 133(1) matter` @desc Which kind of matter is it: shares, debentures, rights or options, contracts, participatory interests, or other securities that the Authority prescribes, of the corporation or of a related corporation?
    `the person contravened section 133(3) in respect of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice not in the form or not given in the time that section 133(3) requires?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(1)(b) the director or chief executive officer intentionally or recklessly contravened section 133(3)` MEANS
    IF `s 134(1) the matter is one that subsection (1) names` `the matter` AND `the person contravened section 133(3) in respect of the notice` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("intentionally or recklessly contravenes section 133(3) in respect of a notice of the particulars of any matter referred to in section 133(1)(a)(i)"), not that anyone else is innocent

-- src:28293 | (c) in purported compliance with section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i),
-- src:28294 | (c)(i), (d)(i) or (f), or section 133(1)(g) in respect of a
-- src:28295 | change in the particulars of any matter referred to in
-- src:28296 | section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) and (f), provides
-- src:28297 | any information which he or she knows is false or
-- src:28298 | misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to
-- src:28299 | whether it is,
@ref s 134(1)(c) (src:28293-28299)
GIVEN
    `the matter` IS A `s 133(1) matter` @desc Which kind of matter is it: shares, debentures, rights or options, contracts, participatory interests, or other securities that the Authority prescribes, of the corporation or of a related corporation?
    `the person in purported compliance provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance, did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(1)(c) the director or chief executive officer in purported compliance provided information known to be false or misleading` MEANS
    IF `s 134(1) the matter is one that subsection (1) names` `the matter` AND `the person in purported compliance provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("provides any information which he or she knows is false or misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is"), not that anyone else is innocent

-- src:28275 | 134.—(1) Any director or chief executive officer of a corporation
-- src:28276 | who —
-- src:28278 | (a) intentionally or recklessly contravenes
-- src:28280 | section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) or (f), or
-- src:28282 | section 133(1)(g) in respect of a change in the particulars
-- src:28284 | of any matter referred to in section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i),
-- src:28286 | (c)(i), (d)(i) and (f);
-- src:28288 | (b) intentionally or recklessly contravenes section 133(3) in
-- src:28289 | respect of a notice of the particulars of any matter referred
-- src:28290 | to in section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) and (f) or of a
-- src:28291 | change in any of those particulars; or
-- src:28293 | (c) in purported compliance with section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i),
-- src:28294 | (c)(i), (d)(i) or (f), or section 133(1)(g) in respect of a
-- src:28295 | change in the particulars of any matter referred to in
-- src:28296 | section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) and (f), provides
-- src:28297 | any information which he or she knows is false or
-- src:28298 | misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to
-- src:28299 | whether it is,
-- src:28301 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:28302 | not exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:28303 | 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further
-- src:28304 | fine not exceeding $25,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:28305 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 134(1) (src:28275-28305)
GIVEN
    `the matter` IS A `s 133(1) matter` @desc Which kind of matter is it: shares, debentures, rights or options, contracts, participatory interests, or other securities that the Authority prescribes, of the corporation or of a related corporation?
    `the person contravened section 133(1) in respect of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person fail to give the written notice that section 133(1) requires for the matter?
    `the person contravened section 133(3) in respect of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice not in the form or not given in the time that section 133(3) requires?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance, did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(1) the director or chief executive officer is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`s 134(1)(a) the director or chief executive officer intentionally or recklessly contravened section 133(1)` `the matter` `the person contravened section 133(1) in respect of the matter` `the contravention was intentional or reckless` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 134(1)(b) the director or chief executive officer intentionally or recklessly contravened section 133(3)` `the matter` `the person contravened section 133(3) in respect of the notice` `the contravention was intentional or reckless` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`s 134(1)(c) the director or chief executive officer in purported compliance provided information known to be false or misleading` `the matter` `the person in purported compliance provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) no paragraph of subsection (1) is met on these facts; subsection (2) may still apply

-- src:28301 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:28302 | not exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:28303 | 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further
-- src:28304 | fine not exceeding $25,000 for every day or part of a day during
-- src:28305 | which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref 2 s 134(1) (the penalty) (src:28301-28305)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 134(1) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $250,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (24 months) or both; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
    Penalty OF 250000, 24, TRUE, 25000

-- src:28309 | (2) Any director or chief executive officer of a corporation who —
-- src:28311 | (a) contravenes section 133(1) or (3); or
-- src:28313 | (b) in purported compliance with section 133, provides any
-- src:28314 | information which is false or misleading in a material
-- src:28315 | particular,
-- src:28320 | in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (1) shall be guilty
-- src:28321 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:28322 | $25,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:28323 | exceeding $2,500 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:28324 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 134(2) (src:28309-28324)
GIVEN
    `the matter` IS A `s 133(1) matter` @desc Which kind of matter is it: shares, debentures, rights or options, contracts, participatory interests, or other securities that the Authority prescribes, of the corporation or of a related corporation?
    `the person contravened section 133(1) in respect of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person fail to give the written notice that section 133(1) requires for the matter?
    `the person contravened section 133(3) in respect of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice not in the form or not given in the time that section 133(3) requires?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance, did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134(2) the director or chief executive officer is guilty of an offence under subsection (2)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person contravened section 133(1) in respect of the matter` OR `the person contravened section 133(3) in respect of the notice` OR `the person in purported compliance provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("contravenes section 133(1) or (3)" or provides false or misleading information), not that anyone else is innocent
        IF `s 134(1) the director or chief executive officer is guilty of an offence under subsection (1)` `the matter` `the person contravened section 133(1) in respect of the matter` `the person contravened section 133(3) in respect of the notice` `the contravention was intentional or reckless` `the person in purported compliance provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (i) "in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (1)": a case within subsection (1) is carved out of this one (a named complement)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

